---
// Fills the image box in a card that has no image. The box decides the format,
// this only fills it. The logo is drawn as a background with space around it, so it is
// whole no matter how narrow the box gets, unlike a photo that is cropped.
//
// The outer element gives the box the same height a 4:3 image would have given it, so that
// cards with and without an image are equally tall. The surface is placed absolutely over the whole box,
// so the box must be positioned (position: relative).
---

<div class="standardbilde">
  <div class="standardbilde-flate"></div>
</div>

<style>
  .standardbilde {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }

  /* Same burgundy as og-image.svg. */
  .standardbilde-flate {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background-color: #541321;
    background-image: url('/ki-norge-logo-hvit.svg');
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: center;
    background-size: contain;
    background-origin: content-box;
    background-clip: border-box;

    /* The padding controls the size: the logo is 5:1 wide, so "contain" always hits
       the width, and the content box width becomes the logo width. The side padding is 30 and
       not 20 percent because Sara wanted the text smaller, which gives 40 rather than 60 percent
       of the box, that is two thirds of the original size. */
    padding: 15% 30%;
  }
</style>
